WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:07.265
Chef greeted the kids in the farmyard with a basket.

2
00:00:07.266 --> 00:00:10.099
"Please pick some spinach from the garden.

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.324
We're making cheesy spinach balls today.

4
00:00:13.325 --> 00:00:17.490
Later you can feed my little helpers."

5
00:00:17.491 --> 00:00:23.317
Izzie was curious. "Do you mean the chickens and goats?"

6
00:00:23.318 --> 00:00:31.207
"No. You've never met these helpers," Chef said.

7
00:00:31.208 --> 00:00:35.222
The kids went to the garden and picked spinach.

8
00:00:35.223 --> 00:00:39.556
"I wonder who Chef's helpers are," Izzie said.

9
00:00:39.557 --> 00:00:43.088
"Maybe he got a pig!" Bobby said.

10
00:00:43.089 --> 00:00:48.087
Nina laughed. "Pigs aren't little!

11
00:00:48.088 --> 00:00:55.631
And they're not helpers, are they?"

12
00:00:55.632 --> 00:00:59.141
*** In the kitchen Bobby read the

13
00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:03.245
recipe. "We have to cook the spinach in olive

14
00:01:03.246 --> 00:01:07.504
oil." Nina poured olive oil into a pan and turned on the

15
00:01:07.505 --> 00:01:11.426
burner. They dumped the spinach into the pan and stirred

16
00:01:11.427 --> 00:01:14.568
it. The leaves turned dark

17
00:01:14.569 --> 00:01:17.403
green. Chef removed the pan from the

18
00:01:17.404 --> 00:01:19.728
burner. "We'll let the spinach

19
00:01:19.729 --> 00:01:23.223
cool. Then we'll chop it and wring it out to dry it

20
00:01:23.224 --> 00:01:26.120
off." Chef handled the

21
00:01:26.121 --> 00:01:31.423
spinach. Izzie preheated the oven to 175 degrees

22
00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:36.625
Celsius. Nina grated Parmesan cheese, and Bobby chopped green

23
00:01:36.626 --> 00:01:40.432
onions. Izzie was still thinking about Chef's mystery

24
00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.960
helpers. "Chef, what do the helpers

25
00:01:43.961 --> 00:01:46.184
do?" "They keep my garden

26
00:01:46.185 --> 00:01:49.850
healthy." "Are they rabbits?" Nina

27
00:01:49.851 --> 00:01:53.229
asked. "Rabbits eat vegetables," Jason

28
00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:56.690
said. "Gardeners chase away

29
00:01:56.691 --> 00:02:00.192
rabbits." Izzie measured three-quarters cup of bread

30
00:02:00.193 --> 00:02:03.209
crumbs. She poured them into a

31
00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:07.592
bowl. Jason cracked an egg and beat it before adding

32
00:02:07.593 --> 00:02:10.824
it. Nina put in two tablespoons of

33
00:02:10.825 --> 00:02:14.680
yogurt. Chef added the chopped

34
00:02:14.681 --> 00:02:18.768
spinach. "Do your helpers like spinach balls?" Izzie

35
00:02:18.769 --> 00:02:23.489
asked. Chef smiled. "They love raw

36
00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:28.189
spinach." Chef melted butter in a pan.

37
00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:31.325
Then he poured it into the bowl.

38
00:02:31.326 --> 00:02:34.556
The kids added the cheese and green onion.

39
00:02:34.557 --> 00:02:39.523
Bobby sprinkled in half a teaspoon of paprika and pepper.

40
00:02:39.524 --> 00:02:44.271
Then they stirred all the ingredients together.

41
00:02:44.272 --> 00:02:48.396
"Form small balls with your hands," Chef said.

42
00:02:48.397 --> 00:02:54.299
"Squeeze them so they don't fall apart."

43
00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:57.880
The kids placed the balls on a baking sheet.

44
00:02:57.881 --> 00:03:01.832
Chef put them in the oven.

45
00:03:01.833 --> 00:03:06.222
"Now can we feed your helpers?" Izzie asked.

46
00:03:06.223 --> 00:03:12.181
"Soon." Chef brought out a pail with a lid.

47
00:03:12.182 --> 00:03:14.102
"Here's their food."

48
00:03:14.103 --> 00:03:17.097
The kids peered inside.

49
00:03:17.098 --> 00:03:21.833
There were vegetable and fruit scraps, coffee grounds, and crushed eggshells.

50
00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:26.001
There were also torn pieces of cardboard.

51
00:03:26.002 --> 00:03:30.486
"It sure looks like pig food!" Bobby said.

52
00:03:30.487 --> 00:03:37.124
Ding! The spinach balls were finally ready.

53
00:03:37.125 --> 00:03:39.813
They each tried one.

54
00:03:39.814 --> 00:03:44.972
"Yum, cheesy and crunchy!" Nina said.

55
00:03:44.973 --> 00:03:49.489
Izzie looked at Chef. "Is it time?"

56
00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:55.624
"Yep." Chef led the kids out to the shed.

57
00:03:55.625 --> 00:04:01.549
Inside was a bin with holes in the lid and the sides.

58
00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:03.971
He opened the lid.

59
00:04:03.972 --> 00:04:06.229
The bin was full of dirt.

60
00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:09.608
Chef turned on his phone's flashlight.

61
00:04:09.609 --> 00:04:12.130
Izzie saw something wiggly.

62
00:04:12.131 --> 00:04:18.102
"Earthworms! But how do they help you?"

63
00:04:18.103 --> 00:04:22.814
"After earthworms eat, they produce waste," Chef said.

64
00:04:22.815 --> 00:04:26.423
"Earthworm poop!" Jason said.

65
00:04:26.424 --> 00:04:28.912
"Yep," Chef said.

66
00:04:28.913 --> 00:04:31.861
"Their poop is full of nutrients.

67
00:04:31.862 --> 00:04:34.539
So I add it to the garden soil.

68
00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.102
It makes our plants really healthy."

69
00:04:38.103 --> 00:04:41.030
"Gross!" Bobby said.

70
00:04:41.031 --> 00:04:43.066
But Izzie grinned.

71
00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:47.850
"It's awesome! Can we feed the worms now?"

72
00:04:47.851 --> 00:04:51.486
Chef nodded.

73
00:04:51.487 --> 00:04:54.987
The kids emptied the scraps into the bin.

74
00:04:54.988 --> 00:04:58.608
"There you go, worms," Izzie said.

75
00:04:58.609 --> 00:05:03.954
"Thank you for keeping our garden healthy!"

